Subject: Hardcode field validation status, and repair a mojibake string

Applies to: scriptAtlassianPure2.js  ->  scriptAtlassian2.js
Atlassian source: the widget application bundle the embed loader pulls into
                  the iframe (iframe.js)

1. `fieldValidationStatus` (two occurrences) no longer derives required-ness
   from `getFormFields()`. It is replaced with a fixed literal:
       { summary: true, description: true, attachment: true, email: true }

   THIS IS A CONSTRAINT ON THE JSM PROJECT, not just on this file.
   The widget's request type must expose exactly these four fields. Add a
   required field to it in Jira and the widget will report the form valid,
   submit an incomplete payload, and surface no usable message to the visitor.
   Because the widget no longer validates, our own React forms are the only
   validation a visitor gets - any new entry point must reproduce it.

2. "Can<mojibake>t add attachment" -> "Can not add attachment".
   Not a feature: the pristine bundle was saved through a Latin-1 round trip
   and its apostrophe is corrupted. If these bundles are ever re-vendored as
   UTF-8, drop this hunk rather than carrying it forward.

